          74,
          78,
          76
         ],
         "end": "sweet spot"
        }
       ],
       "max": 82
      }
     },
     "A petrol engine only makes useful power in a band, roughly fifteen hundred to six thousand rpm. The wheels need to go from stopped to very fast."
    ],
    [
     "c03_3",
     {
      "label": "low gear",
      "head": "First gear: *pulling* power",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "gears",
       "r1": 60,
       "r2": 170,
       "label": "LOW GEAR: SLOW BUT STRONG"
      }
     },
     "In first gear, a small gear drives a much bigger one. The wheels turn slowly, but with lots of force to get you moving."
    ],
    [
     "c03_4",
     {
      "label": "high gear",
      "head": "Top gear: *speed*",
      "pose": "cheer",
      "face": "happy",
      "prop": {
       "type": "gears",
       "r1": 110,
       "r2": 110,
       "label": "HIGH GEAR: FAST AND RELAXED"
      }
     },
     "In top gear, the gears are closer in size. The wheels spin fast while the engine stays relaxed on the motorway."
    ],
    [
     "c03_5",
     {
      "label": "the clutch",
      "head": "The *clutch* connects and disconnects",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "clutch"
      }
     },
     "In a manual car, the clutch briefly unhooks the engine from the gearbox, so gears can change without grinding."
    ],
    [
